# Database Migrations with Flask-Migrate

All commands require `--app server` unless `FLASK_APP=server.py` is set in your environment.

---

## One-Time Setup

```bash
flask --app server db init
flask --app server db migrate -m "initial schema"
flask --app server db upgrade
```

---

## Every Future Schema Change

```bash
flask --app server db migrate -m "describe what changed"
flask --app server db upgrade
```

Always review the generated script in `migrations/versions/` before running `upgrade` on production.

---

## Command Reference

| Command               | Purpose                                              |
| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `db init`             | One-time setup — creates the `migrations/` folder    |
| `db migrate -m "msg"` | Auto-generates a migration script from model changes |
| `db upgrade`          | Applies all pending migrations                       |
| `db downgrade`        | Rolls back the last migration                        |
| `db history`          | Lists all migrations in order                        |
| `db current`          | Shows which migration the database is currently on   |
| `db stamp head`       | Marks DB as up-to-date without running migrations    |

---

## ⚠️ Column Renames — Do Manually

Alembic cannot detect column renames. It will generate a `DROP + ADD` instead, which deletes your data. Always write the migration manually for renames using `op.alter_column()`.
